 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 531550,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Given the data 1, 4, 5, 5, and 10, find the standard deviation using the process outlined in the definition.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The formula for standard deviation uses sigma notation where sigma denotes a sum, <i>x</i> represents each data value, <span data-math=\"\\overline x \"></span> represents the mean of the data values, and <i>n</i> is the number of data values.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"s = \\sqrt {\\frac{{\\sum {{{\\left( {x - \\overline x } \\right)}^2}} }}{{n - 1}}} \"></span></p>\n<p>It helps to make a table.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><i>x</i></th>\n<th><span data-math=\"x - \\overline x \"></span></th>\n<th><span data-math=\"x - \\overline x \"></span></th>\n<th><span data-math=\"{(x - \\overline x )^2}\"></span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1 − 5</td>\n<td>−4</td>\n<td>16</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>4 − 5</td>\n<td>−1</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>5 − 5</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>5 − 5</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>10 − 5</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>25</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sum: 25</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Sum: 42</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\overline x  = 25 \\div 5 = 5\"></span></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"s = \\sqrt {\\frac{{\\sum {{{\\left( {x - \\overline x } \\right)}^2}} }}{{n - 1}}}  = \\sqrt {\\frac{{42}}{{5 - 1}}}  = \\sqrt {\\frac{{42}}{4}}  = \\sqrt {10.5}  \\approx 3.240\"></span></p>\n<p>The standard deviation is 3.240.</p>"
    },
    {
